From a8355fa8ce92c0083bf387f846ac71d71d749d11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:46:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(sim,app): turning programs simulate on the field eye
 about their fitted spindle, with meridian parity

plan_program no longer refuses the Turn family. The plan carries the
insert's nose radius and the op's fitted lathe axis (re-fitted with
turning::profile::Frame::about from operation::source_facets - the
generator's own material read), and the field eye (stock_view,
stock_play) cuts each lathe op through the revolved nose stadium about
that axis (Stock::simulate_lathe_about, new LatheAxis in
stock_sim::field_lathe; simulate_lathe keeps world +Z). A chord's
second end is now signed against the first's side, so a parting chord
past centre is the meridian segment it is.

Grooving/parting blades, threading inserts and form gauges refuse by
name (LATHE_BLADE_REFUSAL, the blade-profile sweep is #21). The column
verdict (simulate_document) refuses any lathe program by name
(LATHE_VERDICT_REFUSAL), so the post gate still shows "not judged".
A lathe op's plan radius is its nose (the display cell law).

Readings (debug, 0.5 mm cell, sign at every cell centre two cells
inside the stock against the meridian law written in the test):
facing 438,976 centres / 10,680 cut / 0 misses; facing about an
off-origin axis (3, -2) 0 misses; profile rough+finish 438,976 /
11,992 / 0; multi-pass contour 438,976 / 9,160 / 0; boring 429,777 /
2,904 / 0.

Pinned by: lathe_field_sim (facing_simulates_on_the_field_with_
meridian_parity, a_bar_off_the_origin_is_turned_about_its_own_fitted_
axis, profile_rough_and_finish_simulate_with_meridian_parity,
multi_pass_contour_simulates_with_meridian_parity, boring_simulates_
inside_the_bore_with_meridian_parity, a_grooving_blade_is_refused_by_
name_and_the_verdict_refuses_the_lathe); stock_lathe::a_stated_axis_
off_the_origin_cuts_the_same_meridian.

Fixes #19

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
